# TODO - Shared capability ownership

## Objective

Enforce reuse before new implementations.

## Acceptance

- Keep one canonical shared mechanism with configurable behaviour.
- Use specialised strategies only for real title-specific differences.
- Add regression tests across consumers when shared contracts change.

## Evidence

On 2026-11-24, `cargo validate --no-cache` passed after adding the
canonical `games::timing::StepClock` mechanism. Its interval and per-frame
work budget are configured once per scheduler; `FixedTick` composes different
consumers without forking the implementation. Synthetic counter and motion
consumers verify equivalent simulation under different frame rates, bounded
catch-up without lost time, ordered indices and invalid interval rejection.

The project has no onboarded titles yet. Title-specific specialisations are
therefore deferred until genuine differences can be demonstrated; no original
game parity is claimed. Cross-consumer regression tests protect the public
shared scheduler as its contract evolves.

On 2026-11-25, the first playable title supplied reusable geometry:
sprite rectangles and centered placement moved to games::presentation,
with the IR re-exporting the single shared type. Simpsons ground-shadow
placement uses the engine method. Its normalized touch boundary mapping
moved to games::input::touch, including rejection of invalid extents.
Deterministic tests cover extreme dimensions and ordered touch boundaries
across representative and maximum extents. All 512 scoped engine,
platform and Simpsons all-feature tests passed. This is scoped evidence,
not completion of the ongoing platform migration.

Viewport expansion and evenly distributed HUD anchors are now shared
engine presentation functions. Simpsons retains its own design width and
seat count, while both center and station offsets use the engine math.
Regression cases cover contraction, odd expansion, invalid slot indices,
single-seat centering and maximum u32 extents. The scoped engine,
platform and title run passed 513 tests before the feature-isolation work.

Shared engine input latency bookkeeping now retains the oldest admitted
input per pending tick and consumes applied timestamps once. Simpsons uses
this same ledger for local and remote input measurement. Centered touch
panel transforms moved to the engine with the original rounding policy;
Simpsons supplies its own panel dimensions. New pure tests exercise both
contracts and existing title regressions remain intact. Scoped engine and
title all-feature tests passed 329 executions, and strict Clippy passed.

The engine now owns sparse animation keyframe selection and cyclic tick
calculation. Simpsons retains its own characters, tracks and durations,
but consumes the shared animation implementation. Tests cover missing
frames, track isolation, exact transitions and maximum elapsed ticks.

Animation tracks now accept caller-selected ordered tick types, and cycle
timing accepts integer durations convertible to and from the elapsed tick
representation. Optional-track completeness is shared by Simpsons enemy
and pair animation validation. Deterministic tests cover absent tracks,
required keys, track isolation, durations above 255 and maximum u64 ticks.
The engine passed 113 tests and strict Clippy; Simpsons passed all 223
all-feature tests. Title-specific animation durations remain in the title.

The shared presentation mechanism now owns left-aligned meter geometry,
pixel rectangle membership, configurable solid RGBA mask admission and
checked RGBA row slicing. Simpsons supplies its own colours, coordinates
and health dimensions. Tests cover large extents, out-of-range pixels,
overflowing row offsets and invalid masks. The engine and title passed
115 and 223 scoped tests respectively.

The shared engine now owns padded horizontal camera geometry through
StripViewport. Each title selects its design width, maximum view width
and inset; the engine checks arithmetic and clamps camera travel to the
available strip. Regression cases cover the existing arcade dimensions,
an independently configured 80,000-column view and overflow rejection.
Scoped engine and Simpsons tests passed 116 and 223 executions.
